<title>USA: Thermo Voltek gets $2.5 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Thermo Voltek gets $2.5 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermo Voltek Corp said on Wednesday that its Netherlands-based subsidiary Comtest received a $2.5 million contract to develop a customized electromagnetic compatibility test facility for a customer in Spain.</p>
<p>Comtest would assist in the design and engineering of several large semi-anechoic chambers for Laboratori General d'Assaigs i Investigacions, a part of the General Department of Industry and Energy in Catalunya, Spain. Comtest would also install the chambers at the test facility.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
